# P2-AR-0047 held-out probe output, as captured by heldout/RUN-ALL on cap2-candidate-1
# (commit 0bad524d836f179964ffbac31972856ea6434682, product_code_digest e6332fc7…2220)
PASS D1-b1-content-hash — an edited file is reported stale by content hash before any rebuild
PASS D1-b1-restored — after an incremental rebuild the index is fresh again
PASS D1-b2-affected — renaming a method inside a changed file removes the old symbol and chunk and adds the new ones
PASS D1-b2-stale-edges — an edge owned by an unchanged file is either removed or reported dangling after its target is deleted (remaining=[file:src/web/http.ts], dangling=1)
PASS D1-b3-rename — a renamed file is not duplicated: the old path is gone and only the new one is indexed
PASS D1-b4-embedder — changing the embedding dimension makes the live index incompatible (pin mismatch), not merely out of date
PASS D1-b4-no-mixed — an incompatible semantic state is not silently queried under the new pin
PASS D1-b5-manifest — the index manifest records the embedder's adapter/model/runtime identity, the chunker, the lexical tokenizer, the index version and the repository commit
PASS D1-reclass-detected — a path-map reclassification of unchanged files is detected by freshness (reclassified=['src/app/bases.py', 'src/app/orders.py', 'src/lib.rs', 'src/svc/Ledger.java', 'src/svc/handler.go', 'src/web/client.ts'])
PASS D1-reclass-applied — an INCREMENTAL rebuild applies the reclassification to the unchanged files (namespace=archive, default_retrieval=0)
PASS D1-reclass-retrieval — after the reclassification the archived source is out of default retrieval
